-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Beyond the Ice Palace
  Publisher   Elite Systems, 1988
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Beyond the Ice Palace (1988)(Elite Systems)(128K).z80
  MD5         1c1af4775bc0114f7b94edb7de2d4070

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Note        Original colours with the colour clash removed: the figures are
              Next sprites drawn from the game's own masks and pictures, and
              the scenery keeps its attributes. Original pace (a limiter caps
              the faster drawing) and the original loading screen. With Start
              with 99 lives the display still shows at most nine hearts, as
              the original does. Known issues: sound effects use the same AY
              writes in the same order, but their timing within an update can
              differ from the original by a few milliseconds; one of the eight
              hook sites (a screen-copy caller) was only checked by a direct
              test, not in play. Missing: no Enhanced colour set; not every
              level was played to completion; tested through the loader on
              NextZXOS v2.09, not yet checked on v2.10; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Start with 99 lives
   2  Infinite lives
   3  Immunity
   4  Immune to bats
   5  Infinite spirits

  The archive's POKEs for this release use 48K addresses that do not match
  this 128K version; these five were translated to its code and each one was
  tested.

